## 🎯 Edge-to-Edge & Picture-in-Picture Implementation Scratchpad

## 🔍 Analysis First:

### Understanding the Task Goal:
Implement edge-to-edge display and picture-in-picture (PiP) mode throughout the EventWish app with proper error handling and premium design aesthetics. The app should provide immersive experiences for greeting card viewing/editing while maintaining festive, warm, and engaging Material 3 design standards.

### Linked/Related Files Working Together:
1. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/MainActivity.java** - Main activity for global edge-to-edge setup
2. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/ui/detail/TemplateDetailFragment.java** - Template viewing with WebView (PiP candidate)
3. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/ui/shared/SharedWishFragment.java** - Shared greeting cards (PiP candidate)
4. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/resourse/ResourceFragment.java** - Resource viewing with WebView
5. **app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml** - Activity configurations and permissions
6. **app/src/main/res/values/themes.xml** - Material 3 theme with edge-to-edge support
7. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/utils/EdgeToEdgeManager.java** - New utility for edge-to-edge management
8. **app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/utils/PictureInPictureManager.java** - New utility for PiP management

### Key Design Principles:
- **Immersive Edge-to-Edge**: Full-screen content with adaptive system bars
- **Smart PiP Integration**: Context-aware picture-in-picture for greeting cards
- **Premium Error Handling**: Graceful fallbacks with Material 3 design
- **Festive Aesthetics**: Maintain warm, celebratory design language
- **Accessibility First**: WCAG compliance and inclusive design

